# Independent candidate-to-payload review

Reviewed changes on base 3964847 across ci.yml, selected/export, candidate.prepare, fixtures and README against spec15 same checked artifact/freshness gates. No implementation edits or actual API operations.

No blocking finding. CI changes only the diagnostic upload name to doc-browser-<sha>-<run-id>-<attempt>; paths, uploaded contents, if:always behavior and permissions are unchanged. Failed runs can still preserve diagnostic artifacts, but prepare first verifies successful CI and only then invokes selected using the verified run/attempt/source. selected requires the matching attempt-qualified name and metadata run/source, while independently pinned raw tar and manifest checks remain mandatory. Legacy names are conservatively rejected. The actual export CLI now requires --attempt and the shared fixture drives its -I subprocess coverage.

Independent tests: candidate 8 and artifact/export 8 passed normally and with python -O (16 per mode). Additional probe confirmed failed required CI calls selected zero times. A fully consistent second attempt passed and returned the original tar; old job attempts cannot be rescued by renaming the artifact. Tests cover old run/attempt and legacy names plus failed-CI rejection. Final README was rechecked after the initial stale argument/name observation; it now documents --attempt, qualified names, prepare ordering and the historical status of old uploads.

Artifact naming is a trusted-workflow convention, not standalone proof of a job's upload. Authentication, job-to-upload provenance, successful required gates and freshness immediately before mutation remain host responsibilities. Partial reruns lacking all eight jobs for the selected attempt fail closed under the existing complete-attempt contract. No archived live legacy artifact was relabeled to claim compatibility, no new upload ran, and neither this adapter nor its Candidate grants publication permission, Pages upload identity, current-publication or LKG proof.

Official GitHub context reference checked 2026-09-13: https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/contexts#github-context . run_id remains the workflow run identifier across reruns, while run_attempt identifies the incrementing attempt. This matches the new name components. CI success on the new workflow remains a separate required check.
